<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<class name="InputComponent" inherits="Node" api_type="extension" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot/master/doc/class.xsd">
	<brief_description>
		Binds input actions to callables for a possessed pawn.
	</brief_description>
	<description>
		Handed to [code]Pawn._setup_input_component[/code]. Bindings live as long as the possession does.
		Every query goes through the owning [PlayerController] [PlayerInput], so a pawn only ever sees its own player devices. Reading [Input] directly from a pawn script would move every pawn at once - that is the problem [PlayerInput] exists to solve. When the component has no owning controller, or that controller has no [LocalPlayer], it falls back to the global [Input] singleton, which is what this class did before per-player input existed.
	</description>
